{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalQConnectionExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalQConnectionExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.GaugeTheory","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QDifferentialGeometry","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQConnection.exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQConnection.exists","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-connection-exists.lean#L37-L81","doc":"**Existence of the categorical q-connection.**\n\nIn an `R_q`-linear monoidal category `C`, given the Frobenius–Hopf object\n`A`, the 1-forms object `Ω¹`, the classical connection `∇`, the Reeb\ncontraction `ξ ⌟ ∇`, the canonical 1-form `θ`, and a unit substrate\nparameter `q` (`q · qinv = 1`), there exists a `CategoricalQConnection C`\nwhose underlying objects and classical data are exactly the inputs and\nwhose q-deformed connection morphism is exactly the `R_q`-linear\ncombination `q⁻¹ ∇ + (1 - q⁻¹) (ξ ⌟ ∇) θ`.\n\nSince the q-connection bundles its objects (`A`, `Ω¹` are fields), the\nobject identifications use `=` and the morphism identifications use `HEq`\ntransported along them (the `MassGap` ∃-repackaging pattern, §U4).  The\nexistential pins the `nabla_q` field to the defining formula, so the\nwitness genuinely realises [`def:categorical-q-connection`]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-q-connection-exists","label":"prop:categorical-q-connection-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-connection-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}